PRE-EXISTING a11y defect — NOT caused by NEARS-1686. Observed 2026-08-10 on
emulator-5556, UserApp debug build from
feat/NEARS-1686-tracking-chat-null-guard @ 47ff0410, English, light mode.

Surface: UserApp order_details_screen.dart — the "track order" FloatingActionButton
(child = NAssetImage(Images.trackLocationIcon)) carries no Semantics label, so it
is invisible to label-based drivers AND to screen readers.

Live a11y tree (order #170, status pending) — the FAB is an unlabeled ImageView:

    class=android.widget.ImageView clickable=true bounds=[1128,2254][1296,2422]

ui_find exit codes on that same screen (captured without a pipe, so the code is
ui_find's own):

    [Order Tracking] rc=0 out='672 447'     <-- the details-timeline SECTION HEADING
    [Chat]           rc=1 out=''
    [Call]           rc=1 out=''
    [Track Order]    rc=1 out=''

The trap: `ui_find "Track"` returns rc=0 on this screen, but it has matched the
"Order Tracking" section heading, not the FAB. Tapping it is a no-op that reads
as a successful navigation:

    tap 'Order Tracking' @ 672 447   ->  a11y dump unchanged, still on details

The FAB could only be driven by resolving the last `ImageView clickable=true`
from ui_nodes and tapping its live-resolved centre (1212, 2338).

Impact: TalkBack announces an unlabeled button; QA cannot drive the primary
entry point to order tracking by label. Out of the NEARS-1686 fence
(order_details_screen.dart, not order_tracking_screen.dart) — routed, not filed.
